class:: RatioFamilyOsc
summary:: Language-side family of continuously spread phase-shaped oscillators
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

RatioFamilyOsc is a language-side graph constructor. It creates one signed
Phasor and sine reader per literal ratio. code::spread:: moves ratios in
log-frequency space, while code::skew:: and code::curve:: bend two continuous
phase segments. No dedicated server UGen or optional Quark is required.

The closest vanilla construction is an array of link::Classes/SinOsc:: UGens.
RatioFamilyOsc adds validated ratio spreading, signed phase accumulation, and
a shared two-segment phase-shaping law.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Signed root frequency in hertz.

argument:: ratios
One to 32 positive finite literal ratios.

argument:: spread
Logarithmic spread. Zero produces unison, one preserves supplied ratios, and
negative values move toward reciprocal relationships.

argument:: skew
Input position of the phase breakpoint, clipped to code::0.001..0.999::.

argument:: curve
Quadratic segment bend, clipped to code::-1..1::. Endpoints and cycle
continuity do not move.

argument:: linearFM
Signed frequency offset in hertz applied to every voice after ratio spreading.

argument:: phase
Initial/readout phase in radians.

argument:: mul
Multiplier applied independently to every output.

argument:: add
Offset added to every output after multiplication.

returns::
One audio channel per ratio, in input order.

method:: kr

RatioFamilyOsc is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

subsection:: Discussion

The mapping's output breakpoint is one half cycle. Therefore
code::skew = 0.5:: and code::curve = 0:: are neutral. Construction cost and
server graph size grow linearly with the ratio count.

examples::

code::
(
{ Splay.ar(RatioFamilyOsc.ar(70)) * 0.045 }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
    Splay.ar(
        RatioFamilyOsc.ar(
            51, [1, 7/6, 4/3, 3/2, 7/4, 2],
            spread: LFTri.kr(0.05).range(-0.5, 1.5),
            skew: 0.35, curve: 0.4
        )
    ) * 0.04;
}.play;
)
::

